    linear-gradient(0deg, rgba(0, 45, 58, 0.54), rgba(0, 45, 58, 0.1) 54%);
}

/* THE PHOTO HERO SCRIM IS WEIGHTED TO THE TEXT COLUMN, NOT SPREAD FLAT OVER THE
   WHOLE FRAME. The shared shade above never falls below 0.1 horizontally and
   carries a full-width bottom wash, so on /patio-doors/, /upvc-doors/ and
   /sliding-sash-windows/ â€” the three darkest hero photographs on the site â€” the
   product itself sits under a permanent veil and stops reading.

   The stops below were chosen so the density where the copy actually sits is
   held, not reduced. `.fg-hero__copy` is max-width 820px inside a 1180px
   container, so on a 1440px viewport the eyebrow, H1 and intro occupy roughly
   x=9%..57%, and `.fg-hero--compact` centres them vertically. Compounding the
   two layers, the old effective alpha at the eyebrow band was 0.579 and the new
   one is 0.581; at the tail of the intro it moves 0.425 -> 0.466. Past 74% â€”
   where no hero text can reach â€” it falls from about 0.29 to 0.14 and then to
   nothing, and the bottom wash is shortened from 54% of the height to 32%, so
   the photograph is uncovered exactly where the product is.

   Scoped to `.fg-hero--compact` rather than to `.fg-hero__shade` globally,
   following `.fg-roof-lantern-page .fg-hero__shade` further down this file: the
   home and commercial heroes are composed differently and are not part of this.
   The â‰¤860px override further down still wins on phones and is untouched. */
.fg-hero--compact .fg-hero__shade {
  background:
    linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(0, 45, 58, 0.6) 0%, rgba(0, 45, 58, 0.48) 56%, rgba(0, 45, 58, 0.14) 80%, rgba(0, 45, 58, 0) 95%),
    linear-gradient(0deg, rgba(0, 45, 58, 0.4) 0%, rgba(0, 45, 58, 0) 32%);
}

/* THE EYEBROW COLOUR IS NO LONGER MOBILE-ONLY. `#68d798` lived inside the
   `@media (max-width: 860px)` block below and nowhere else, so above 860px the
   compact hero eyebrow fell back to `--color-accent` (#2eac66) over a
   photograph and failed WCAG AA on all fifteen photo-hero routes. Only the
   colour is unscoped here; the `margin: 0` in that block is mobile layout for
   the stacked heading and stays there.

   READ THIS BEFORE CALLING IT FIXED: this raises every route but does not clear
   4.5:1 on the brightest photographs on its own. FULL-SITE-AUDIT-2026-08-13.md
   :1828 measures the accent green at 1.39:1 on /aluminium-bifold-doors/ and
   records that #68d798 still only reaches about 2.3:1 there at the old scrim.
   The audit's own recommendation is `#ffffff`, which is a change of brand
   identity on fifteen heroes and is the owner's call, not this file's. */
.fg-hero--compact .fg-hero__heading .eyebrow {
  color: #68d798;
}

