}

.fg-product-quote-embed {
  padding: clamp(2.4rem, 5vw, 4rem) 0;
  background: transparent;
}

.fg-product-quote-embed__grid {
  display: grid;
  /* Widened from 0.34fr on 2026-08-10. The copy column measured 293px, and the
     heading beside it is a display size, so long product labels broke one word
     to a line. The iframe loses about 50px and does not care. */
  grid-template-columns: minmax(260px, 0.4fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
  gap: clamp(1rem, 2vw, 1.5rem);
  align-items: stretch;
}

.fg-product-quote-embed__copy,
.fg-product-quote-embed__card {
  border: 1px solid rgba(0, 45, 58, 0.12);
  border-radius: 8px;
  background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);
  box-shadow: var(--fg-shadow-lg);
}

.fg-product-quote-embed__copy {
  display: grid;
  align-content: center;
  padding: clamp(1.2rem, 2vw, 1.65rem);
}

/* This heading interpolates the product label, so its length is not fixed: it
   runs from "Design and price your uPVC Doors online." to "...your Aluminium
   Sliding Patio Doors online.", 40 characters to 59, across 21 routes. At the
   old 3rem in a 293px column that longest one broke into six lines with
   "Sliding" alone on one of them, and the owner reported it as messed up.

   Two constraints were fighting: `max-width: 13ch` AND a column narrower than
   13ch resolves to. The cap is gone, the column now does the constraining, and
   the size is set so the WORST label still reads. `balance` evens the rag out
   so short labels do not end on a widow. Check the long routes, not the short
   ones, if you ever change this. */
.fg-product-quote-embed__copy h2 {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 1.95vw, 2.05rem);
  line-height: 1.06;
  text-wrap: balance;
}

