/* ============================================================================
   THE STYLE RANGE IN ONE VIEWPORT, 2026-09-02
   Owner: "make the style range smaller. in one viewport."

   It was 1,234px against an 827px usable viewport at 1440x900 — the section
   plus a sticky 73px header — so a third of it was always below the fold and
   the switcher scrolled away from the doors it switches.

   WHAT THE HEIGHT WAS SPENT ON, measured with Esprit open (the largest
   collection at 43): 249px of section and card chrome, a 179px head, a 533px
   panel, and about 100px of gaps between blocks. Every one of those is cut
   here and nothing is removed from the page.

   THE COLUMN COUNT IS NOT TOUCHED, AND MUST NOT BE. `FIRST_LOOK` in `main.js`
   is 20, and ten columns is the only count that makes twenty doors exactly two
   full rows. Fifteen columns would show one row of fifteen and five orphans
   beside ten empty cells. It is pinned at `repeat(10, ...)` above 1200px so
   `auto-fill` cannot drift off that number and break the arithmetic.

   THE DRAWINGS GET SHORTER, NOT NARROWER. They are `object-fit: contain` in
   their cell, so capping the art height letterboxes a portrait door rather
   than distorting it: the same drawing, smaller, still 102px of cell to sit
   in. That is the whole saving on the panel.

   Desktop only. A phone has never had this section in one viewport and the
   instruction is a desktop one; the rails and the two-column grid below 861px
   are left exactly as they are.
   ========================================================================= */

@media (min-width: 861px) {

  /* ---- The card was chrome the section did not need --------------- */

  /* The quiz moved to the tail of the page, so this surface has held nothing
     but the contact sheet since. A border and 88px of padding around a
     section that is already the only thing in its own `<section>`. */
  .generated-page--composite-doors .fg-choose__surface {
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
    border-radius: 0;
    background: none;
    box-shadow: none;
  }

  .generated-page--composite-doors > .fg-choose {
    padding-block: clamp(24px, 2.4vw, 34px);
  }

  /* ---- The head ---------------------------------------------------- */

  .generated-page--composite-doors .fg-cds__head {
    max-width: 62rem;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  /* `max-width: none` is the line that matters. The heading scale caps this
     h2 at 24ch, which at 32.8px wrapped a 640px string onto two lines inside
     a 992px box and cost 35px for nothing. */
  .generated-page--composite-doors .fg-cds__head h2 {
    max-width: none;
    margin: 0.2rem 0 0.25rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 2.5vw, 2.05rem);
    line-height: 1.06;
  }

  .generated-page--composite-doors .fg-cds__head .eyebrow { margin-bottom: 0.35rem; }

  /* Its own 15.36px top and bottom margins, inside a block whose gap already
     separates it from the switcher. */
  .generated-page--composite-doors .fg-cds__head > p:not(.eyebrow) {
    max-width: 96ch;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  /* The blocks inside were spaced for a section with room to spare. */
  .generated-page--composite-doors .fg-cds {
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(0.7rem, 1.1vw, 0.85rem);
  }

  /* ---- The panel head --------------------------------------------- */

  .generated-page--composite-doors .fg-cds__panel-head {
    max-width: 96ch;
    margin-bottom: clamp(0.45rem, 0.9vw, 0.65rem);
  }

  .generated-page--composite-doors .fg-cds__panel-title {
    margin-bottom: 0.2rem;
    font-size: 1.02rem;
  }

  .generated-page--composite-doors .fg-cds__panel-intro { font-size: 0.9rem; }

  /* ---- The doors --------------------------------------------------- */

  /* Ten, always. See the note above: twenty is two rows only at ten. */
  .generated-page--composite-doors .fg-cds__grid {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(10, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 7px;
  }

  .generated-page--composite-doors .fg-cds-door__link {
    gap: 0.25rem;
    padding: 0.45rem 0.35rem 0.4rem;
  }

  /* THE ONE REAL SAVING, AND IT HAS TO BE `max-height`. The first attempt set
     `height: 76px` on the art box and `height: 100%` on the drawing, and the
     drawings rendered 168px tall, straight through the name and into the row
     below: the art box measured 76px but the image's computed height came back
     `168.469px`, so the percentage never resolved against it. `max-height` on
     the same selector provably does apply — it is what took the old 230px cap
     off — so the cap goes there and the row sizes itself to the result.
     `object-fit: contain` was already set, so a portrait door letterboxes
     inside its cell: shorter, never distorted. */
  .generated-page--composite-doors .fg-cds-door__art { min-height: 0; }

  .generated-page--composite-doors .fg-cds-door__link img { max-height: 72px; }

  /* Two reserved lines existed so a wrapping name could not push its row out
     of line. One line and a smaller face fits every name in this range, and
     the reservation stays — it is just a shorter one. */
  .generated-page--composite-doors .fg-cds-door__name {
    min-height: 1.3em;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  /* THE CUE RESERVED A ROW IT ONLY USED ON HOVER. Eighteen px per tile, on
     every tile, to say nothing until the pointer arrives. It overlays the name
     on hover instead, which is the same affordance for no height. */
  .generated-page--composite-doors .fg-cds-door__link {
    position: relative;
  }

  .generated-page--composite-doors .fg-cds-door__cue {
    position: absolute;
    right: 0.35rem;
    bottom: 0.4rem;
    left: 0.35rem;
    font-size: 0.6rem;
    background: rgba(247, 249, 248, 0.94);
  }

  /* ---- The note ---------------------------------------------------- */

  /* Two lines at 100ch, one at the container's own width, and it is the last
     20px between the big collections and a single viewport. Capping the
     measure here was costing more than it bought: this is one closing
     sentence under a grid, not a column of body copy. */
  .generated-page--composite-doors .fg-cds__note {
    max-width: none;
    margin-top: 0;
    font-size: 0.86rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .generated-page--composite-doors .fg-cds__filters {
    padding-block: 0.4rem;
  }
}

